  "body": "# Corrective Apple Silicon test preview 3\n\nExperimental native Apple Silicon build for **macOS 14 or newer**. Keep a separate Fiji test installation and use the accompanying clean-Mac handoff. This is bounded tested coverage, not a certificate for every GAT workflow or biological dataset.\n\n## Why update from preview 2\n\nFull multiplex-registration tests found a pre-existing Java result/landmark-handling defect that preview 2 retained: later-round marker exports could remain unaligned and physical calibration was reset. **Do not use preview 2 multiplex exports for quantitative work.** Preview 3 preserves distinct landmarks, restores them onto the correct images, selects verified fresh transform results, and carries reference calibration into both export stacks.\n\nThe unchanged native acceptance test now passes both SIFT and forced-MOPS routes. Independent reopening of actual saved TIFFs and ROI archives verifies exact SIFT marker interiors, MOPS residual MSE 0.180\u20130.360 versus 2,751\u20134,313 before correction, correct landmark shifts and calibrated outputs. The 18 inputs, five harness sources and 97 runtime JAR identities are identical between failed and corrected runs. No registration parameters or acceptance assertions were relaxed.\n\n[Retained before/after multiplex evidence](https://github.com/justinvassantachart/GutAnalysisToolbox/blob/f5b814b4a8f784246d60df88032cee037ca8fd29/native-inference/validation/multiplex-full/results/mac-ab046cb/README.md)\n\n## What is included\n\n- `GAT-2.0.1-apple-silicon.3-macos-arm64-preview.zip`: one fork plugin plus isolated native ARM64 TensorFlow and Template Matching workers, complete required worker source/licenses, installation guide and workflow matrix\n- Matching checksum and build information; the whole archive source is `bb897c237732cf8569a1515eb8d7ed69feb2ab31`\n- A separate unchanged original `1870d9e` baseline bundle, for an isolated comparison Fiji installation\n- `M1-CHATGPT-HANDOFF-v5.md`: full instructions from a bare Mac, including official Fiji/bundled Java, updater sites, model/engine setup, fair original/fork tests, physical GPU/GUI checks and structured reportback\n- A manual multiplex fixture add-on with the exact public synthetic inputs and saved references. The earlier corrected general test kit 2.1 remains usable for neuron/calcium/SIFT/Template Matching controls\n\n## Tested boundaries\n\nActual same-host native Mac GAT calls record original TensorFlow/OpenCV failures and passing fork neuron/alignment outputs. Accepted-dialog calcium and ganglia commands run on **both** original and fork; the ganglia RDF scaling correction intentionally changes masks, so old-mask equality is not claimed. Original sources remain unchanged. Full official native Fiji download/updater/engine/model/dashboard/neuron/alignment/ganglia acceptance has passed separately.\n\nThe new multiplex acceptance is synthetic service/command coverage. Natural SIFT failure-to-MOPS fallback, unavailable Block Matching, computation-time cancellation, biological quality and every desktop interaction remain separate checks. Hosted Macs expose no usable OpenCL device; physical-M1 EDF/spatial/CLIJ kernels remain required. The original automatic calcium ROI and batch StackReg options are unimplemented. Optional JPEG-XR is a separate tested add-on, with container/importer/metadata checks still needed.\n\nNeuron runtime consistency is close rather than universally pixel-identical. The preserved 371 Linux comparisons have equal counts but include small boundary/outline differences and one local moved-center counterexample. Inspect the per-cell evidence rather than treating counts or a green coverage job as scientific equivalence.\n\nA separate native hosted-M1 run completed all 40 source-labeled public test\nfiles (39 unique inputs, with one training overlap). Counts and centers match\nin all cases, 39 canonical rasters/measurements match, 37 raw label rasters match,\nand all 15 subtype rasters match. A single Hu polygon loses one boundary pixel;\nsubpixel contours are not universally identical. Full legacy tensors/paint\norder are unavailable for most cases, and the report preserves that boundary.\n\nNo upstream PR has been opened. Older release tags/assets are preserved.\n\n## Installation\n\nRead the v5 handoff asset before running. Verify every SHA-256. Install the fork overlay only into the identified test Fiji data root; keep both worker folders outside Fiji's global `jars` and `plugins`. Do not upgrade models/engines, mix architectures, disable Gatekeeper or substitute algorithms to suppress errors. Preserve the unchanged baseline copy and all failed-run evidence.\n\n## Exact build and checksums\n\nNative build and paired test: https://github.com/justinvassantachart/GutAnalysisToolbox/actions/runs/37382657593 (successful), source `bb897c237732cf8569a1515eb8d7ed69feb2ab31`, clean working tree.\n\n- Core ZIP: 203,286,850 bytes; SHA-256 `5c746a31c65727779566ed9b9a1bfdd4966167504bce7ee95bd4878ed2159d03`\n- Core plugin JAR: SHA-256 `0bb1c33b452fcd607f13291532e103199223d947eeec605a91dcac03dc047792`\n- Original baseline ZIP: 1,664,352 bytes; SHA-256 `3c7f3289f714f3789b9dad47dd4f9e7032812b8886c43705a97853888d50ce86`\n- General test kit2.1 (unchanged fixture bytes): SHA-256 `979d818165e677215824808834391ad80b70866c86ead5da2ae8830e022a2d55`\n- Multiplex manual add-on: 231,740 bytes; SHA-256 `31e15feb164b38c5ab42f9ff6cdceee5507c4563cea648a2b85ae9f38524a04c`\n\nThe general kit retains historical source/evidence from preview2; use the new handoff for installation and current status. Its historical title does not mean installing old core binaries. The optional JPEG-XR package remains available with the exact unchanged hashes and full source/license archive in preview2's assets; it is separate from the multiplex correction.\n\n"
